from major retailers to luxury stores  and small businesses organized retail  crime also known as orc has been on the  rise for several years with a spike in  incidents over the last few weeks  orc incidents involve any form of retail  theft by an organized group from  shoplifting to cargo theft  recently there has been a spike in smash  and grab organized retail crime where  large groups smash display windows and  can steal thousands of dollars in  merchandise within minutes  i probably saw 50 to 80 people in like  ski mass crowbars night like a bunch of  weapons they were looting the nordstrom  right here nearly three-fourths of us  retailers said they saw a spike in orc  in 2020 according to a national retail  security survey and many said the  pandemic has played a role as covid  influenced the way america shops  everybody was buying their goods online  so it created this incredible increase  in demand for online products organized  until crime organizations stepped up to  fill that demand  ben dugan has been following trends in  retail crime for 30 years and has worked  with cvs for the last four years to  investigate orc incidents  he says members of orc groups can target  as many as 15 to 20 stores in a single  day and often resell the stolen goods as  a third-party seller on various online  marketplaces well the biggest challenge  when dealing with illicit sellers on  online marketplaces first and foremost  is who they are they do not have to  provide their real names or addresses or  banking information or information that  that any legitimate business  would provide as cvs health's top  investigator dugan said he solved 27  cases of e-commerce crime in 2020 alone  amounting to nearly 50 million dollars  worth of goods earlier this year a  bipartisan group of senators introduced  the inform consumers act which would  require e-commerce platforms to verify  high-volume third-party seller  information  ultimately making it more difficult to  sell stolen goods from locking up  products and ramping up physical  security measures to installing gps  tracking on products stores are finding  new ways to combat potential orc  incidents specifically smash and grab  robberies  our retailers are doing a lot  especially this holiday season as always  the number one concern for the retail  community and industry is to keep our  employees and our customers safe  [Music]
 

